<title>USA: TVA's Tenn. Watts Bar 1 nuke at 20 pct power -- NRC.</title>
<headline>TVA's Tenn. Watts Bar 1 nuke at 20 pct power -- NRC.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>TVA Nuclear's 1,170 megawatt (MW) Watts Bar 1 nuclear unit in Spring City, Tenn., is operating at 20 percent power, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission said in its Thursday morning report.</p>
<p>The unit on Wednesday exited its maintenance outage, which began on September 27.</p>
<p>TVA's 1,148 MW Sequoyah unit 2 in Soddy Daisy, Tenn., shut last Friday due to a coolant pump leak, is still off line. Although an exact date could not be given, the company said earlier this week that the outage would be short-term.</p>
<p>-- New York Power Desk +212-859-1628</p>
